IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p1`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 7 (industrial injuries benefits), Part VI: industrial death benefit, paragraphs 14 to 21. The converter dropped the paragraph
-- numbers. They follow the eight headings after "Part VI": 14 Introductory, 15 Widow's benefit (entitlement), 16 (rate), 17 Widower's benefit,
-- 18 Deceased's family, 19 Limits of entitlement in respect of children, 20 Death of person with constant attendance allowance, 21 Pulmonary disease.
-- The text's own citations confirm 15, 16, 18 and 19 ("paragraph 16 below" in 15(2); "paragraph 18 below" in 16(2)(a) and 19; "paragraph 19 below" and
-- "paragraphs 15 and 16 above" in 18(1)). A "Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph N" amount is the omitted Schedule 4 figure, taken as an input.
-- This Part "only has effect in relation to deaths before 11th April 1988" (14(1)): every rule here is asked about such a death.

§ `Schedule 7 Part VI -- industrial death benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 14 -- introductory`

-- 14(1): "This Part of this Schedule only has effect in relation to deaths before 11th April 1988."
-- A death on or after 11 April 1988 is outside the closed scope ("only"): FALSE. A death before it is inside the scope the sentence states: TRUE (reading (e), NOTES.md: "only" is read
-- as fixing the scope, as Part III paragraph 10(1) states its scope without the word; the other reading is that "only" is a necessary condition and the answer inside is NOTHING).
-- src:5571 | (1) This Part of this Schedule only has effect in relation to deaths before 11th April 1988.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 14(1) (src:5571)
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 14(1) this Part has effect in relation to the death` MEANS
    IF `the day of the death` LESS THAN Date 11 4 1988
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- reading (e), mine: "only has effect in relation to deaths before 11th April 1988" is read as stating the Part's scope, so a death before that day is inside it
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only has effect in relation to deaths before 11th April 1988"

-- 14(1A): "No claim may be made for industrial death benefit after the coming into force of this sub-paragraph." The day it came into force
-- is not in the text, so it is an input.
-- src:5572 | (1A) No claim may be made for industrial death benefit after the coming into force of this sub-paragraph.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) (src:5572)
GIVEN `the day of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the day this sub-paragraph came into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day this sub-paragraph came into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the commencement day is not in the text
    WHEN JUST commencement THEN
        IF `the day of the claim` GREATER THAN commencement
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No claim may be made for industrial death benefit after the coming into force of this sub-paragraph"
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a claim not barred by this sub-paragraph is decided by the other paragraphs

-- 14(2): "the deceased" is the person in respect of whose death industrial death benefit is claimed or payable. The definition says "means", so it is closed.
-- src:5573 | (2) In this Part of this Schedule “the deceased” means the person in respect of whose death industrial death benefit is claimed or payable.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 14(2) (src:5573)
GIVEN `industrial death benefit is claimed or payable in respect of the person's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 14(2) the person is the deceased` MEANS
    IF `industrial death benefit is claimed or payable in respect of the person's death`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the deceased” means the person in respect of whose death industrial death benefit is claimed or payable"

§§ `Paragraph 15 -- widow's benefit (entitlement)`

-- 15(1) and (4): the widow of the deceased is entitled to death benefit if at his death either (a) she was residing with him or (b) she was receiving
-- or entitled to receive, or would but for the relevant accident have been receiving or entitled to receive, from him periodical payments for her
-- maintenance of not less than the prescribed amount. 15(4): such payments are only payments provided or procured by the deceased (whether from him or
-- from another), and "entitled" means entitled under a court order, trust or agreement which the widow has taken reasonable steps to enforce.
-- src:5575 | (1) The widow of the deceased shall be entitled to death benefit if at his death either—
-- src:5576 | (a) she was residing with him; or
-- src:5577 | (b) she was receiving or entitled to receive, or would but for the relevant accident have been receiving or entitled to receive, from him periodical payments for her maintenance of not less than the prescribed amount.
-- src:5580 | (4) In this paragraph—
-- src:5581 | (a) references to a widow receiving or being entitled to receive payments from the deceased are only to her receiving or being entitled to receive (whether from him or from another) payments provided or procured by the deceased; and
-- src:5582 | (b) “entitled” means, in relation to any such payments, entitled under any order of a court, trust or agreement which the widow has taken reasonable steps to enforce.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) and (4) (src:5575-5577) (src:5580-5582)
GIVEN `the person is the widow of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she was residing with him at his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments for her maintenance were provided or procured by the deceased (whether from him or from another)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she was receiving the payments at his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she was entitled to the payments under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she would but for the relevant accident have been receiving or entitled to receive the payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly amount of the payments for her maintenance` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` MEANS
    IF `the person is the widow of the deceased` AND (`she was residing with him at his death` OR maintained)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The widow of the deceased shall be entitled to death benefit if at his death either (a) ... or (b) ..." (a failed "if")
    WHERE
        maintained MEANS `the payments for her maintenance were provided or procured by the deceased (whether from him or from another)` AND (`she was receiving the payments at his death` OR `she was entitled to the payments under an order of a court, trust or agreement which she has taken reasonable steps to enforce` OR `she would but for the relevant accident have been receiving or entitled to receive the payments`) AND (`the weekly amount of the payments for her maintenance` AT LEAST `the prescribed amount`)

-- 15(2): in the case of a widow, death benefit is a pension commencing from the death and payable (at the 16 rate) for life or until she remarries or
-- forms a civil partnership. The result is about the entitled widow only.
-- src:5578 | (2) In the case of a widow, death benefit shall be a pension commencing from the death of the deceased and payable, at the weekly rate for the time being applicable under paragraph 16 below for life or until she remarries or forms a civil partnership.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) (src:5578)
GIVEN `the widow is entitled to death benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day of the deceased's death` IS A DATE
      `the day she remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day she died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the widow is entitled to death benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the pension is "in the case of a widow", who is entitled under 15(1)
        IF `the widow is entitled to death benefit` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the entitlement under 15(1) is not answered
        IF day LESS THAN `the day of the deceased's death`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a pension commencing from the death of the deceased" is a stated start; the sub-paragraph does not say a pension is unpayable before it
        IF remarried
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payable ... until she remarries or forms a civil partnership"; "until" read as ending the pension on the day of the remarriage (fork F11, NOTES.md)
        IF afterDeath
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable ... for life" is a stated period; the sub-paragraph does not say the pension is unpayable after the widow's death
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        remarried MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day she remarried or formed a civil partnership`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST end THEN day AT LEAST end
        afterDeath MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day she died`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST end THEN day GREATER THAN end

-- 15(3): "A pension under this paragraph shall not be payable for any period during which the beneficiary is living as a married couple with a person
-- whom she is not married to or in a civil partnership with."
-- src:5579 | (3) A pension under this paragraph shall not be payable for any period during which the beneficiary is living as a married couple with a person whom she is not married to or in a civil partnership with.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 15(3) (src:5579)
GIVEN `the beneficiary is living as a married couple with a person whom she is not married to or in a civil partnership with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 15(3) the pension may be payable for the period` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiary is living as a married couple with a person whom she is not married to or in a civil partnership with`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be payable for any period during which the beneficiary is living as a married couple with a person whom she is not married to"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not be payable" is a bar and no grant

§§ `Paragraph 16 -- widow's benefit (rate)`

-- 16(2)(b): the higher permanent rate applies "where the widow was over the age of 50 at the deceased's death or was over the age of 40 at the end of the
-- period for which she was entitled to such an allowance". Ages are the K2 answers (s 173(a)); the second limb needs such an allowance to have been paid.
-- src:5587 | (b) where the widow was over the age of 50 at the deceased’s death or was over the age of 40 at the end of the period for which she was entitled to such an allowance; or
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) (src:5587)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person was over 50 at the deceased's death` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `she was entitled to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons for some period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person was over 40 at the end of the period for which she was entitled to such an allowance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 173(a) the person was over 50 at the deceased's death` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `she was entitled to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons for some period`
            THEN `s 173(a) the person was over 50 at the deceased's death`
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 173(a) the person was over 40 at the end of the period for which she was entitled to such an allowance`
                  WHEN JUST over40 THEN IF over40 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 173(a) the person was over 50 at the deceased's death`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- 16(1), (2) and (3): the weekly rate of the pension is, for "the period of 26 weeks next following the deceased's death", the initial rate; after that
-- period the higher permanent rate for any period (a) for which she is entitled, or treated by regulations as entitled, to an allowance for children
-- or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18, (b) as above, (c) where she was permanently incapable of self-support at the death, or (d) while pregnant by
-- the deceased; in any other case the lower permanent rate. 26 weeks is 182 days. The pension commences from the death (15(2)), so the 26 weeks are read as
-- beginning with the day of the death; the reading that starts them on the next day leaves the day of the death without a rate (NOTES.md, fork F10).
-- src:5584 | (1) The weekly rate of a pension payable under paragraph 15 above shall, for the period of 26 weeks next following the deceased’s death, be the initial rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 10.
-- src:5585 | (2) The weekly rate of the pension shall, after the end of that period, be the higher permanent rate specified in that paragraph—
-- src:5586 | (a) for any period for which the widow is entitled, or is treated by regulations as entitled, to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 below; or
-- src:5587 | (b) where the widow was over the age of 50 at the deceased’s death or was over the age of 40 at the end of the period for which she was entitled to such an allowance; or
-- src:5588 | (c) where the widow at the deceased’s death was permanently incapable of self-support; or
-- src:5589 | (d) while the widow is pregnant by the deceased.
-- src:5590 | (3) After the end of the period of 26 weeks referred to in sub-paragraph (1) above, the weekly rate of the pension shall, in any case not within sub-paragraph (2) above, be the lower permanent rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 10.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 16 (src:5584-5590)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day of the deceased's death` IS A DATE
      `sch 4 pt V para 10 the initial rate in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 10 the higher permanent rate in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 10 the lower permanent rate in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the widow is entitled, or is treated by regulations as entitled, to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 for the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the widow at the deceased's death was permanently incapable of self-support` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the widow is pregnant by the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF day LESS THAN `the day of the deceased's death`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the pension commences from the death
        IF (Day day) MINUS (Day `the day of the deceased's death`) LESS THAN 182
            THEN `sch 4 pt V para 10 the initial rate in pounds`   -- NOTHING when the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
        IF `the widow is entitled, or is treated by regulations as entitled, to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 for the day` OR `the widow at the deceased's death was permanently incapable of self-support` OR `the widow is pregnant by the deceased` OR `the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN `sch 4 pt V para 10 the higher permanent rate in pounds`
        IF `the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the age answer is missing and no other limb of 16(2) holds
        OTHERWISE `sch 4 pt V para 10 the lower permanent rate in pounds`

§§ `Paragraph 17 -- widower's benefit`

-- 17(1) and (2): the widower of the deceased is entitled to death benefit if at her death he (a) was being wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would but for the
-- relevant accident have been so maintained, and (b) was permanently incapable of self-support. The benefit is a pension at the Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 11 rate,
-- from her death, for life.
-- src:5592 | (1) The widower of the deceased shall be entitled to death benefit if at her death he—
-- src:5593 | (a) was being wholly or mainly maintained by her or would but for the relevant accident have been so maintained; and
-- src:5594 | (b) was permanently incapable of self-support.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) (src:5592-5594)
GIVEN `the person is the widower of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at her death he was being wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would but for the relevant accident have been so maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at her death he was permanently incapable of self-support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` MEANS
    IF `the person is the widower of the deceased` AND `at her death he was being wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would but for the relevant accident have been so maintained` AND `at her death he was permanently incapable of self-support`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The widower of the deceased shall be entitled to death benefit if at her death he (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "if")

-- src:5595 | (2) In the case of a widower, death benefit shall be a pension at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 11 commencing from the death of the deceased and payable for life.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) (src:5595)
GIVEN `the widower is entitled to death benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day of the deceased's death` IS A DATE
      `the day the widower died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `sch 4 pt V para 11 the weekly rate of the widower's pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt VI para 17(2) the weekly rate of the widower's pension on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the widower is entitled to death benefit` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST 0   -- no pension: the text gives none to a person outside 17(1)
        IF `the widower is entitled to death benefit` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the entitlement under 17(1) is not answered
        IF day LESS THAN `the day of the deceased's death`
            THEN JUST 0   -- "commencing from the death of the deceased"
        IF endedBy `the day the widower died`
            THEN JUST 0   -- "payable for life"
        OTHERWISE `sch 4 pt V para 11 the weekly rate of the widower's pension in pounds`   -- NOTHING when the Schedule 4 table is omitted
    WHERE
        endedBy ending MEANS
            CONSIDER ending
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST end THEN day GREATER THAN end

§§ `Paragraph 18 -- the deceased's family`

-- 18(1): where at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit for one or more children or qualifying young persons, then for any period for which (a) the
-- widow is entitled (i) to death benefit (other than a gratuity) under paragraphs 15 and 16 and (ii) to child benefit for the child, or (b) a person prescribed is entitled to
-- child benefit for the child, the widow or that person is entitled, for each such child, to an allowance at the Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 12 weekly rate. "Subject to
-- paragraph 19": satisfying the conditions is no more than NOTHING until paragraph 19 and 18(2) are applied (the seat layer composes them).
-- src:5597 | (1) Subject to paragraph 19 below, where at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit in respect of one or more children or qualifying young persons, then, for any period for which—
-- src:5598 | (a) the widow of the deceased is entitled—
-- src:5599 | (i) to death benefit (other than a gratuity) under paragraphs 15 and 16 above; and
-- src:5600 | (ii) to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person or one or more of those children or qualifying young persons; or
-- src:5601 | (b) such other person as may be prescribed is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person or one or more of those children or qualifying young persons,
-- src:5602 | the widow or, as the case may be, the person so prescribed shall be entitled in respect of that child or qualifying young person, or in respect of each respectively of those children or qualifying young persons, to death benefit by way of an allowance at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 12.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) (src:5597-5602)
GIVEN `at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit in respect of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the widow of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the widow is entitled to death benefit (other than a gratuity) under paragraphs 15 and 16 for the period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to child benefit in respect of the child for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit in respect of the child`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit" is a "where", not an "if"
        IF NOT `the person is entitled to child benefit in respect of the child for the period`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for any period for which ... is entitled to child benefit" (a failed "while": marginal reading (a))
        IF `the person is a person prescribed for this purpose`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph 19 below"; the allowance is cut back by paragraph 19 and paragraph 5
        IF NOT `the person is the widow of the deceased`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the widow or, as the case may be, the person so prescribed shall be entitled" names two persons and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the widow is entitled to death benefit (other than a gratuity) under paragraphs 15 and 16 for the period`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                  WHEN JUST entitled THEN IF entitled THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph 19 below"

-- src:5597 | (1) Subject to paragraph 19 below, where at his death the deceased was entitled to child benefit in respect of one or more children or qualifying young persons, then, for any period for which—
-- src:5598 | (a) the widow of the deceased is entitled—
-- src:5599 | (i) to death benefit (other than a gratuity) under paragraphs 15 and 16 above; and
-- src:5600 | (ii) to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person or one or more of those children or qualifying young persons; or
-- src:5601 | (b) such other person as may be prescribed is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person or one or more of those children or qualifying young persons,
-- src:5602 | the widow or, as the case may be, the person so prescribed shall be entitled in respect of that child or qualifying young person, or in respect of each respectively of those children or qualifying young persons, to death benefit by way of an allowance at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 12.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) (src:5597-5602)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to the allowance for the children` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of children and qualifying young persons in respect of whom the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 12 the weekly rate of the allowance in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the weekly allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person is entitled to the allowance for the children`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the entitlement is not answered
    WHEN JUST entitled THEN
        IF entitled
        THEN CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 12 the weekly rate of the allowance in pounds`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
             WHEN JUST each THEN JUST (each TIMES `the number of children and qualifying young persons in respect of whom the person is entitled`)
        ELSE JUST 0

-- 18(2): "Paragraph 5 above applies in relation to an allowance under this paragraph as it applies in relation to an increase of benefit under paragraph 4 above."
-- It is Part I's paragraph 5(1) read for the allowance (and its 5(2) for the contributions limb).
-- src:5603 | (2) Paragraph 5 above applies in relation to an allowance under this paragraph as it applies in relation to an increase of benefit under paragraph 4 above.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 18(2) (src:5603)
GIVEN `the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 18(2) the allowance for the child may be payable` MEANS
    `sch 7 pt I para 5(1) the increase for the child may be payable` `the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` `the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied`

§§ `Paragraph 19 -- limits of entitlement in respect of children and qualifying young persons`

-- 19: where two or more persons satisfy the conditions in respect of the same death for an allowance under paragraph 18 for a period, (a) not more than one is entitled for the
-- period in respect of the same child; (b) where the deceased leaves a widow or widower who is entitled to death benefit as such and satisfies the conditions, she or he is
-- entitled in respect of that child; (c) subject to (b), regulations may provide priority (inert, machinery). For a person who is not the widow or widower the answer is
-- FALSE if the widow or widower meets (b), and NOTHING otherwise (regulations decide).
-- src:5605 | Where two or more persons satisfy the conditions, in respect of the same death, for receipt of an allowance or allowances under paragraph 18 above for any period—
-- src:5606 | (a) not more than one of those persons shall be entitled for that period to such an allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person;
-- src:5607 | (b) where the deceased leaves a widow or widower, then for any period for which she or he is entitled to death benefit as the deceased’s widow or widower and satisfies the conditions for receipt of such an allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person, she or he shall be entitled to the allowance in respect of that child;
-- src:5608 | (c) subject to sub-paragraph (b) above, regulations may make provision as to the priority in any prescribed circumstances of two or more persons satisfying the said conditions.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 19 (src:5605-5608)
GIVEN `two or more persons satisfy the conditions for an allowance under paragraph 18 for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the widow or widower of the deceased, is entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another of those persons is the widow or widower of the deceased, is entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `two or more persons satisfy the conditions for an allowance under paragraph 18 for the period`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where two or more persons satisfy the conditions"
        IF `the person is the widow or widower of the deceased, is entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `another of those persons is the widow or widower of the deceased, is entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) not more than one of those persons shall be entitled ... in respect of the same child", and (b) names the widow or widower
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(c) ... regulations may make provision as to the priority"

§§ `Paragraph 20 -- death of a person with constant attendance allowance`

-- 20(1) to (3): a person who dies when (a) entitled to an increase under section 104 of a disablement pension of not less than the Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 2(a) amount, or
-- (b) would have been so entitled but for in-patient treatment, "is to be regarded for the purposes of entitlement to industrial death benefit as having died as a result of
-- the injury in respect of which the disablement pension was payable". 20(2): the increase is only a payment by way of increase of a disablement pension, not a payment for
-- constant attendance under paragraph 7(2)(b) of Schedule 8. 20(3): this does not affect death benefit where the death was before 26 July 1971.
-- A person who meets neither (a) nor (b) is outside the "If": FALSE (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)); a death before 26 July 1971 is the flat negative of 20(3): FALSE.
-- src:5610 | (1) If a person dies at a time when—
-- src:5611 | (a) he is entitled to an increase under section 104 above of a disablement pension and the amount of the increase is not less than the amount which at that time is specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a); or
-- src:5612 | (b) he would have been so entitled but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution,
-- src:5613 | he is to be regarded for the purposes of entitlement to industrial death benefit as having died as a result of the injury in respect of which the disablement pension was payable.
-- src:5614 | (2) The reference in sub-paragraph (1) above to an increase under section 104 above includes only a payment by way of increase of a disablement pension, and in particular does not include any payment for constant attendance under paragraph 7(2)(b) of Schedule 8 to this Act.
-- src:5615 | (3) Sub-paragraph (1) above does not affect death benefit where the death occurred before 26th July 1971.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 20 (src:5610-5615)
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the person was entitled to an increase under section 104 of a disablement pension, being a payment by way of increase of a disablement pension and not a payment for constant attendance under paragraph 7(2)(b) of Schedule 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the increase` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 2(a) the amount specified for constant attendance` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the person would have been so entitled but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 20 the person is regarded as having died as a result of the injury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day of the death` LESS THAN Date 26 7 1971
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (1) above does not affect death benefit where the death occurred before 26th July 1971"
        IF `the person would have been so entitled but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the person was entitled to an increase under section 104 of a disablement pension, being a payment by way of increase of a disablement pension and not a payment for constant attendance under paragraph 7(2)(b) of Schedule 8`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person dies at a time when— (a) he is entitled to an increase under section 104 ... or (b) he would have been so entitled but for" (a failed "if"; neither limb is met)
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 2(a) the amount specified for constant attendance`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text
                  WHEN JUST least THEN IF `the amount of the increase` AT LEAST least THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person dies at a time when— (a) ... the amount of the increase is not less than the amount which at that time is specified" (a failed "if"; limb (b) was not met either)

§§ `Paragraph 21 -- pulmonary disease`

-- 21(1) to (3): if a person dies as a result of a pulmonary disease and (a) was entitled, for a period that includes the date of death, to disablement pension or gratuity in respect of
-- pneumoconiosis, byssinosis or pneumoconiosis accompanied by tuberculosis, and (b) the extent of the disablement was assessed for such a period at not less than 50 per cent.,
-- then (subject to (2)) the death is treated, for this Part, as caused by the disease in respect of which the benefit was payable. 21(2): unless regulations provide otherwise, (b) is
-- treated as unsatisfied where, had the deceased's physical condition at the time of the assessment been normal apart from those diseases, the extent would have been assessed at
-- under 50 per cent. 21(3): this does not affect death benefit where the death was before 30 March 1977. The extent of disablement is Schedule 6's answer (seam S21).
-- A person who fails (a) or (b), or whose (b) is treated as unsatisfied by 21(2), is outside the "If": FALSE (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)); a death before 30 March 1977 is the flat negative of 21(3): FALSE.
-- src:5617 | (1) If a person dies as a result of any pulmonary disease and—
-- src:5618 | (a) he was entitled, for a period which includes the date of his death, to disablement pension or gratuity in respect of pneumoconiosis or byssinosis or pneumoconiosis accompanied by tuberculosis; and
-- src:5619 | (b) the extent of the disablement in respect of which the benefit was payable was assessed for such a period at not less than 50 per cent.,
-- src:5620 | then, subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, his death shall be treated, for the purposes of this Part of this Schedule, as having been caused by the disease in respect of which the benefit was payable.
-- src:5621 | (2) Unless regulations provide otherwise, the requirements of paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) above shall be treated as unsatisfied in a case where, had the physical condition of the deceased at the time of the assessment been normal, apart from the diseases mentioned in paragraph (a) of that sub-paragraph, the extent of the disablement in question would have been assessed at less than 50 per cent.
-- src:5622 | (3) This paragraph does not affect death benefit where the death occurred before 30th March 1977.
@ref sch 7 pt VI para 21 (src:5617-5622)
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the person died as a result of a pulmonary disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was entitled, for a period which includes the date of the death, to disablement pension or gratuity in respect of pneumoconiosis or byssinosis or pneumoconiosis accompanied by tuberculosis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the extent that would have been assessed had the physical condition of the deceased at the time of the assessment been normal, apart from those diseases` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day of the death` LESS THAN Date 30 3 1977
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph does not affect death benefit where the death occurred before 30th March 1977"
        IF NOT (`the person died as a result of a pulmonary disease` AND `the person was entitled, for a period which includes the date of the death, to disablement pension or gratuity in respect of pneumoconiosis or byssinosis or pneumoconiosis accompanied by tuberculosis`)
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person dies as a result of any pulmonary disease and— (a) he was entitled, for a period which includes the date of his death, to disablement pension or gratuity" (a failed "if")
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the assessment is Schedule 6's answer and none was given
                  WHEN JUST assessed THEN
                      IF assessed LESS THAN 50
                      THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the extent of the disablement ... was assessed for such a period at not less than 50 per cent., then" (a failed "if": requirement (b) is not met)
                      ELSE CONSIDER `the extent that would have been assessed had the physical condition of the deceased at the time of the assessment been normal, apart from those diseases`
                           WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sub-paragraph (2) turns on a hypothetical assessment that was not given
                           WHEN JUST normal THEN IF (normal LESS THAN 50) AND NOT `regulations provide otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements of paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) above shall be treated as unsatisfied" (a failed "if": requirement (b) is treated as not met)
